@startuml sequence_diagram_role_based_menu
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - WEB03 Role-Based Menu (menu built from the current roles after login or page reload)

actor User as "Client / User"
participant Shell as "SPA Shell\n(WEB01 / WEB02 layout)"
participant Auth as "AuthProvider\n(AA03, extended)"
participant Menu as "NavigationMenu"
participant Policy as "navigationPolicy"
participant API as "authApi / apiClient"
participant Routes as "AuthRoutes\nGET /auth/me"
participant AuthMW as "AuthMiddleware"
participant Service as "UserService"
database DB as "Database\n(Persistence)"

note over User, DB
    Starts after a successful local (AA01) or Google (AA02) login, or when the SPA is
    (re)loaded and a token is stored (AA04). Roles are NEVER decoded from the JWT and
    NEVER chosen by the user: the only source is GET /api/v1/auth/me (AA03).
    While roles are not confirmed, only PUBLIC sections are shown (fail closed).
end note

User -> Shell : opens / reloads the SPA (or login succeeded)
activate Shell
Shell -> Auth : loadCurrentUser()
activate Auth
Auth -> Auth : status = "loading"; currentUser = null

Shell -> Menu : render()
activate Menu
Menu -> Policy : getVisibleSections({ status: "loading" })
activate Policy
Policy --> Menu : PUBLIC sections only\n(catalogue, privacy notice, login)
deactivate Policy
Menu --> User : public menu (no protected option yet)
deactivate Menu

alt A) No token stored
    Auth -> Auth : status = "guest"
    note right of Auth : Guest navigation; interaction ends

else B) Token stored
    Auth -> API : getCurrentUser()
    activate API
    API -> Routes : GET /api/v1/auth/me\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n(skipAuthFailureHandler = true)
    activate Routes
    Routes -> AuthMW : verifyToken(req, res, next)
    activate AuthMW
    AuthMW -> Service : resolveActor(token)
    activate Service
    Service -> DB : SELECT ... FROM users WHERE id = $1
    activate DB
    DB --> Service : row (roles, active)
    deactivate DB
    note right of Service : token, account and roles checks\ndetailed in AA03 (SD 2 / SD 3)
    note over API, Auth
        /auth/me answers are mapped by AuthProvider directly (table A, 3.4):
        the global 401/403 handler is NOT invoked, so no branch below
        can start another /auth/me request (BR 13). Every error branch ends here.
    end note

    alt B1) Token invalid / user deleted (401) or roles not confirmable (5xx, network error)
        Service --> AuthMW : throw AppError (401 / 500)
        AuthMW --> API : 401 / 500 { error: { message, status } }
        API --> Auth : error
        Auth -> Auth : clear(): discard token (AA04);\nstatus = "guest"
        Auth -> Menu : state changed
        activate Menu
        Menu -> Policy : getVisibleSections({ status: "guest" })
        Policy --> Menu : PUBLIC sections only
        Menu --> User : public menu + "Please sign in again."
        deactivate Menu

    else B2) Account inactive or without any role (403, AA03)
        Service --> AuthMW : throw AppError (403)
        AuthMW --> API : 403 { error: { message: "Account is not active" |\n"No active role is assigned to this account", status: 403 } }
        API --> Auth : error 403
        Auth -> Auth : clear(): discard token;\nstatus = "denied"; deniedMessage = error.message
        Auth -> Menu : state changed
        activate Menu
        Menu -> Policy : getVisibleSections({ status: "denied" })
        Policy --> Menu : PUBLIC sections only
        Menu --> User : public menu + AccessDeniedPage(deniedMessage)
        deactivate Menu

    else B3) Active account with roles (200)
        Service --> AuthMW : AuthenticatedActor { sub, email, roles }
        AuthMW -> Routes : next() (req.user = actor)
        Routes -> Service : getCurrentUser(req.user)
        Service --> Routes : UserResponseDTO
        Routes --> API : 200 OK { id, name, email,\nroles: ["CUSTOMER", "MANAGER"], active: true, ... }
        API -> API : parseCurrentUser(body) (AA03 D10)
        API --> Auth : UserResponseDTO
        Auth -> Auth : currentUser = user;\nstatus = "authenticated"
        Auth -> Menu : state changed
        activate Menu
        Menu -> Policy : getVisibleSections(auth)
        activate Policy
        loop for each section in SECTIONS
            alt section.access == "public"
                Policy -> Policy : keep
            else section.access == "guestOnly" (login)
                Policy -> Policy : drop (already authenticated)
            else section.access == "protected"
                Policy -> Auth : hasAnyRole(...section.roles)
                Auth --> Policy : true / false
                Policy -> Policy : keep only if true
            end
        end
        Policy --> Menu : visible sections
        deactivate Policy
        Menu -> Menu : group by SectionGroup;\nskip empty groups; i18n labels (WEB02)
        Menu --> User : role-based menu
        deactivate Menu
        note right of User
            Example [CUSTOMER, MANAGER] = UNION of both roles:
            Catalogue, Privacy notice, My privacy & consents,
            Restaurant management (customers, products, categories,
            allergens, pizza sizes, component types, predefined
            pizzas, stock), Kitchen (viewer, configurations),
            Planning. No Administration group.
            Example [EMPLOYEE]: Catalogue, Privacy notice,
            Products (read-only), Kitchen viewer.
        end note
    end
    deactivate Service
    deactivate AuthMW
    deactivate Routes
    deactivate API
end

deactivate Auth
deactivate Shell

@enduml